IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cor-deaths`

-- Coroners Act 1996 (WA), a death in the family -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_coroners-act-1996_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Life facts are from the workbench scenario au/wa/cradle-to-grave-chloe/facts.json: c086 (2052-08-19) Graham Harding
-- dies at 82 at home; the funeral director registers the death; a cremation permit; "s 17 (reportable deaths: not this
-- one)". Sue, his wife, survives him; his will (c087) makes Chloe executor. That the death was expected and from natural
-- causes, that his GP will certify the cause under s 44 of the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998, and that
-- Sue lived with him, are ASSUMED for the cases; the scenario does not say. Variants change one fact each.

§ `fixtures`

